<title>USA: Weyerhaeuser Q1 share declines.</title>
<headline>Weyerhaeuser Q1 share declines.</headline>
<dateline>FEDERAL WAY, Wash. 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Weyerhaeuser Co AND SUBSIDIARIES</p>
<p>					First Quarter</p>
<p>			  13 Weeks	 13 Weeks	Percent</p>
<p>			  Ended	    Ended	Increase or</p>
<p>		     March 30, 1997  March 31, 1996  (Decrease)</p>
<p>Per common share:</p>
<p>Earnings before</p>
<p>  special charge  $    0.22	   $    0.72	    (69)</p>
<p>Less: Effect of</p>
<p>  special charge (1)  (0.12)		    -		-</p>
<p> Net earnings     $    0.10	   $    0.72	    (86)</p>
<p> Net sales	 $2,608,000	  $2,605,000		-</p>
<p>Earnings before income</p>
<p>taxes and special</p>
<p> charge	     $  72,000	   $ 222,000	    (68)</p>
<p>Less: Income taxes   26,000		80,000	    (68)</p>
<p>Earnings before</p>
<p> special charge	46,000	     142,000	    (68)</p>
<p>Less: Effect of</p>
<p> special charge (1)  25,000		     -		-</p>
<p>Net earnings	$  21,000	    $142,000	    (85)</p>
<p>Avg shares	    198,516	     198,195</p>
<p>(All data in 000s except per share amounts) NOTE: The 1997 special charge is the net of losses from anticipated consolidation, closure or disposition of certain recycling facilities, the completed permanent closure of the corrugated medium machine at Longview, Wash, and the sale of Shemin Nurseries, partly offset by interest income from a favorable federal income tax decision related to timber casualty losses in eruption of Mount St. Helens in 1980.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
